Usage: hostid [OPTION]

Print the numeric identifier of the current host.
Print a 32-bit identifier, in hexadecimal, for the current host.
On Windows, this is derived from the machine GUID.

OPTIONS:
                 print machine identifier
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
